      "lineNbr": 631,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-06T16:59:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t know if we would be having a struct with call backs that could be modified or not. We tend to make things like that const.  Doing this would allow an implementer to change any of the _entry, _run and _exit functions to do what they want instead of our base mechanism.",
      "parentUuid": "dd9ab1a0_6469d94a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 631,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 631,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "343e01b5373fbbd418f7bcbe882d21f4b1d95f53",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8eaa9093_83c7e271",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/usbc/tc/snk.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 631,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-06T17:17:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not certain what the best approach would be here.  I\u0027m tempted to say that states represent the spec, and therefore should be the same for everyone.  But I suppose we certainly have ended up with tricky little \"but I need my board to call this driver function during this type of exit\" before.  \n\nSo I suppose I worry about devs needing to add their corner cases into the common code versus devs maintaining multiple copies of almost identical functions to get their corner cases working.  Neither is ideal.",
      "parentUuid": "31ad61b8_bbe5aae0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 631,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 631,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "343e01b5373fbbd418f7bcbe882d21f4b1d95f53",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1787b30_896ad743",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/usbc/tc/snk.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 631,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-06T17:40:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At first I thought this was the right thing to do but making the board level specific code require duplication of all of this spec code seems unreasonable.\n\nIf the different ports have to do different functionality beyond normal state code that is spec defined, that code tends to require a specific location for the code to work properly. Adding a lot of function pointers would be a reasonable way to do this and not use override.  Seems like it could get ugly real fast.  It would have to be adjustable to possibly be different for the different ports in case some ports have different capabilities or need special handling.",
      "parentUuid": "8eaa9093_83c7e271",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 631,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 631,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "343e01b5373fbbd418f7bcbe882d21f4b1d95f53",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
